+  none or prev-inst; literal policy names.
+
+``semantics.weight`` (string)
+  period or sample (default period).
+
+``semantics.zero_fill`` (string)
+  none or sampled-functions; these are literal policy names, not absence markers.
+
+``throttle`` (string)
+  Unknown: throttle records are not part of the admitted text grammar.
+
+``tool`` (object)
+  Tool identity and invocation.
+
+``tool.arguments`` (array)
+  Full argv in original order, with null for an empty token.
+
+``tool.arguments[]`` (null | string)
+  One argument token, or null for an explicitly empty token.
+
+``tool.version`` (string)
+  LLVM version string.
+
+``verdict`` (object)
+  Conversion outcome and optional threshold results.
+
+``verdict.conversion`` (string)
+  ok or failed; conversion validity, not performance benefit.
+
+``verdict.failure_stage`` (null | string)
+  load/parse/identity/generate/boundary/write/commit on failure; null on success.
+
+``verdict.fallback_callback_count`` (uint64)
+  Number of shared-code failure callback invocations (zero or one).
+
+``verdict.identity`` (string)
+  Same final conservative grade as identity.grade.
+
+``verdict.lost_ratio_check`` (string)
+  not_evaluated, unknown, exceeded or not_exceeded; overflow is unknown.
+
+``verdict.reason`` (null | string)
+  Original failure text (parser diagnostics verbatim), null on success.
+
+``verdict.sample_threshold_check`` (string)
+  not_evaluated, unknown, passed or failed, with threshold precedence above.
+
+``verdict.sampling_adequacy`` (string)
+  insufficient for a failed sample threshold or exceeded LOST check; otherwise unknown.
+
+``verdict.usable_ratio_check`` (string)
+  not_evaluated, unknown, passed or failed, with threshold precedence above.
+
+``warnings`` (array)
+  Distinct diagnostic codes in lexical order; original stderr remains separate.
+
+``warnings[]`` (object)
+  Array element with the child fields below; parent ordering and absence rules apply.
+
+``warnings[].code`` (string)
+  Stable warning identifier listed below.
+
+``warnings[].message`` (string)
+  Human-readable explanation, not a machine decision key.
+
+Warning codes
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+
+``W_CONSTANT_PERIOD``
+  All input periods are equal; caller must confirm fixed-period collection.
+
+``W_DUPLICATE_FUNCTION_START``
+  Existing DWARF loader encountered duplicate function starts.
+
+``W_DWARF_RECOVERABLE``
+  Existing recoverable DWARF diagnostic.
+
+``W_DWARF_WARNING``
+  Existing DWARF warning.
+
+``W_DWO_MISSING``
+  Split DWARF information is incomplete.
+
+``W_EMPTY_DENSITY``
+  Existing density analysis has no usable density positions.
+
+``W_IDENTITY_UNVERIFIED``
+  Missing necessary identity evidence was explicitly allowed.
+
+``W_LARGE_COUNT``
+  Generated counts exceed UINT32_MAX; consumers can saturate branch weights.
+
+``W_LOST_MAY_INCLUDE_SIDEBAND``
+  Visible loss may include mapping/other sideband records.
+
+``W_LOST_RATIO_OVERFLOW``
+  L+S cannot be represented by uint64; report ratio unknown and do not fail that check.
+
+``W_LOST_RATIO_UNKNOWN``
+  Configured visible LOST ratio unavailable or undefined.
+
+``W_LOW_DENSITY``
+  Existing density heuristic recommends more samples.
+
+``W_MD5_IGNORED``
+  Non-extbinary writer ignores use-md5.
+
+``W_NO_DWARF_FUNCTIONS``
+  No DWARF functions were loaded.
+
+``W_TARGET_COUNT_UNKNOWN``
+  Configured target count unavailable before its check.
+
+``W_USABLE_RATIO_UNKNOWN``
+  Configured usable ratio unavailable before its check.
+
+Known limitations
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+Same-name static functions are merged by the existing name-based profile map;
+coverage.name_merged_functions and its top list expose that behavior, not fix
+it. Inline non-leaf frames with line zero still follow existing behavior pending
+validation. No automatic threshold defaults are selected. LOST is an input-wide
+proxy, may include sideband records, does not include every loss source, and
+cannot prove mapping completeness. Missing IDs, inode reuse with unknown
+generation, profiling skid, PMU multiplexing, and nonrepresentative workloads
+can weaken the result. Profiles with different event units, normalization,
+aggregation or build identity must not be treated as interchangeable. Kernel
+and module generation, direct perf.data input, probe builds and production
+scale/performance qualification remain outside this admitted mode.
